{"id":"build","duration":70.73,"voice":"Juniper","segments":[{"t":0,"cap":"In Tableau or Power BI, start by asking what one row of the file is."},{"t":5.54,"cap":"Tableau sums a measure by default. That is right for sales, and wrong for a value that repeats on every row, like a campus's enrollment listed on every course section: take it once, with the maximum or the average."},{"t":22.71,"cap":"To count records, count rows, or count distinct IDs when a record can appear more than once."},{"t":29.08,"cap":"Then make the chart answer the question, and finish it with the design checklist."},{"t":34.88,"cap":"A title that says what the chart shows. Labeled axes with units. Bars that start at zero and are sorted. Color only when it carries a variable. And no chart junk."},{"t":47.89,"cap":"Last, give every number a sanity check: could it be true? In Map Gallery, maps that added up the running totals gave Butler County more than seven million cases, in a county of fewer than four hundred thousand people."},{"t":64.39,"cap":"Save a packaged Tableau workbook, or a Power BI file, so the data travel with it."}],"items":[{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":0.25,"x":44,"y":30,"h":54,"text":"Before you drag anything","d":0.84,"big":true,"color":"red"},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":2.95,"x":44,"y":84,"h":44,"text":"what is one row of the file?","d":0.98},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":5.54,"x":44,"y":128,"h":44,"text":"Tableau sums by default","d":0.81},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":10.99,"x":44,"y":172,"h":44,"text":"repeated value?","d":0.53,"color":"blue"},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":18.88,"x":78,"y":216,"h":44,"text":"take it once: MAX or AVG","d":0.84,"color":"blue"},{"k":"sketch","page":0,"t":5.54,"name":"sumTrap","box":{"x":500,"y":96,"w":430,"h":414},"phases":[10.99,18.88]},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":22.71,"x":44,"y":260,"h":44,"text":"count rows, or count","d":0.7},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":24.86,"x":78,"y":304,"h":44,"text":"distinct IDs","d":0.5},{"k":"page","page":1,"t":29.08},{"k":"hand","page":1,"t